meta {
  name: Pastes
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  The happy paths, in order. These requests chain: **Create paste** stores the new id in
  `{{pasteId}}` and **Get paste** reads it back, so run the folder rather than a single
  request.

  Two behaviours here are worth watching rather than skimming:

  - **The `Location` header is compared against the id in the body.** `RouteOptions.LowercaseUrls`
    is on, and it lowercases generated links whole — route values included. Paste ids are
    case-sensitive base64url, so a `Location` built by link generation points at an id that
    does not exist. That regression is what this assertion exists to catch.
  - **A burn-after-reading paste is gone the instant it is read**, and the second read is
    an ordinary 404 — indistinguishable from an id that never existed, which is the point.
  - **`neverExpires: true` reports `expiresAt: null`**, not a far-future timestamp — see
    "Create paste that never expires".
}
